  "About": {
    "heading": "To designing the future",
    "story": "I’ve always felt like a bit of a misfit.\n\nCurious, restless, and never quite good at accepting “that’s just how it is.”\n\nI've always had trouble fitting into a single box, often feeling like some imposter\n\nI spent my early twenties jumping between medicine, architecture, research, and building things that may or may not ever work.\n\n(with a few failed ventures sprinkled in between)\n\nI’ve changed \"careers\" more than once.\n\nBut it's usually because I found something new I couldn’t stop obsessing about.\n\nAnd right now, that thing is product design. \n\nI'm completely addicted to the craft.\n\nThere's still so much to learn.\n\nThe world is moving fast.\n\nAnd the future can feel uncertain.\n\nBut despite all this, I've never felt more empowered to learn, create, and build things that might make a difference.\n\nMaybe being a misfit isn't so bad after all.\n\nMaybe the beauty of design is that we don't have to accept the world exactly as it is.\n\nWe get to imagine what it could become.\n\nAnd right now, the possibilities feel endless.\n\nSo to all artists, designers, and builders –\n\nMan, what a time to be alive.\n\nTo designing the future.\n\n- DL",
